# 7. String Testing Methods

These methods return **Boolean values**: `True` or `False`.

## `startswith()`

Checks whether the string starts with a specific substring.

```python
print("python".startswith("py"))
# True
```

## `endswith()`

Checks whether the string ends with a specific substring.

```python
print("python".endswith("on"))
# True
```

## `isalpha()`

Returns `True` if all characters are alphabetic.

```python
print("Hello".isalpha())
# True
```

## `isalnum()`

Returns `True` if all characters are letters or numbers.

```python
print("abc123".isalnum())
# True
```

## `islower()`

Checks whether all applicable characters are lowercase.

```python
print("hello".islower())
# True
```

## `isupper()`

Checks whether all applicable characters are uppercase.

```python
print("HELLO".isupper())
# True
```

## `isspace()`

Checks whether all characters are whitespace.

```python
print(" ".isspace())
# True
```

## `istitle()`

Checks whether the string is in title case.

```python
print("Hello World".istitle())
# True
```

## `isidentifier()`

Checks whether the string is a valid Python identifier.

```python
print("variable1".isidentifier())
# True
```

